  "title": "A Two-Coloring of the Edges of KG(11,3) with No Monochromatic Triangle",
  "batch_label": "85",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For the ordinary red-blue edge-coloring problem on the three-uniform Kneser graph, KG(11,3) admits a complete two-coloring of its 4,620 edges in which none of its 15,400 triangles is monochromatic. Consequently R_3^KG(3,3) >= 12. This does not decide the KG(12,3) case, so the frozen original exact-value problem remains unresolved with value in {12,13}.",
